@node CMacs Graphcore
@chapter CMacs Graphcore: the shared graph model and layout solver

@file{cmacs/graphcore/} is the graph engine every cmacs graph
visualiser sits on.  It owns the node/edge store, the CSR adjacency,
the force-directed solver, three closed-form layouts, position
tweening and hierarchical collapse.

It is @emph{not} a @option{--with-cmacs-*} option.  It has no
user-visible surface and no dependency beyond glib, so it is compiled
in whenever something that needs it is enabled --- today
@ref{CMacs Roamgraph}.  @code{configure.ac} sets
@code{HAVE_CMACS_GRAPHCORE} on that basis.

Two consumers want the same maths, and neither difference reaches the
solver: it deals in ids, groups, degrees and positions, and knows
nothing about where any of them came from.  Keeping it shared means a
new layout, a smoother transition or a solver fix is written once.

